/code-review high, loop U9-late1 round 2, branch-scoped (late range 65e8256d..c240859e)

I found 10 problems on `2026-09-26-tool-config-hygiene`. The most serious: the upstream Flutter ignore template, which the Flutter pack now asks for, contains `*.lock`. Every Flutter repo shaped this way would silently stop tracking the mise lockfile and `pubspec.lock`.

- **Checked:** `p:plugins:check`, `inventory --check` and `marketplace --check` all pass. I fetched the upstream templates from github/gitignore `main` to confirm findings 1–3. Findings 1–3 and 6–8 are new since the earlier review rounds.
- **Still unfixed from earlier rounds:** findings 4, 5, 9 and 10 were raised before and are still open. The first three were not in the run log's contested list; the review logs I read don't show what was decided on them.
- **Left out:** the stale `site/`, `installer/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/**` and "eleven passes" docs, because unit U10 still owns them.

